1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Princess Knight,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Thirty-Second Episode
The Silver Ship

15
00:01:53,101 --> 00:01:55,217
Silverland.

16
00:01:55,261 --> 00:01:59,493
Silverland, whose name
means "the land of silver."

17
00:02:00,061 --> 00:02:02,336
Well...
Many centuries ago,

18
00:02:02,461 --> 00:02:05,339
Silverland was
so rich in silver.

19
00:02:05,461 --> 00:02:08,498
...that many armies
fought to conquer it.

20
00:02:16,381 --> 00:02:19,453
The King, who wanted to keep
all the silver for himself,

21
00:02:19,501 --> 00:02:21,412
waged many wars.

22
00:02:21,461 --> 00:02:24,692
As a result,
the country was always in turmoil.

23
00:02:24,781 --> 00:02:27,249
...and the people suffered greatly.

24
00:02:28,181 --> 00:02:30,649
But suddenly
a knight appeared...

25
00:02:30,701 --> 00:02:32,851
in all-silver armor.

26
00:02:33,421 --> 00:02:36,015
He robbed the King
of all his silver.

27
00:02:36,061 --> 00:02:38,734
...and with it he made
a silver ship,

28
00:02:38,781 --> 00:02:40,897
which then sank in a swamp

29
00:02:42,781 --> 00:02:46,057
The mystery of the ship
is written in this sentence:

30
00:02:46,421 --> 00:02:50,209
"The silver swamp sleeps quietly
under three half-moons.

31
00:02:50,261 --> 00:02:53,253
From the circles of water
rises a silver ship.

32
00:02:53,301 --> 00:02:56,179
...and a silver knight
shouts to the sky:

33
00:02:56,221 --> 00:02:58,781
'The moon! The moon can help me!
The moon can give me strength!'"

34
00:02:58,821 --> 00:03:04,293
And time passed
and the legend was forgotten

35
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:19,211
I wonder when that damn guy
will stop reading standing up!

36
00:03:19,261 --> 00:03:21,900
anything else
interesting?

37
00:03:24,661 --> 00:03:27,221
How dare you
dust my head?

38
00:03:27,261 --> 00:03:30,253
You've been there so long
that I mistook you for a book!

39
00:03:30,301 --> 00:03:32,019
Oh, yeah?

40
00:03:34,461 --> 00:03:36,816
I can't see anymore! I can't see anymore!

41
00:03:36,861 --> 00:03:38,852
Damn you!

42
00:03:39,021 --> 00:03:41,251
So you want war?!
Fine, you'll have it!

43
00:03:47,741 --> 00:03:49,459
Fire!

44
00:03:49,501 --> 00:03:52,857
Take this! And this! And this!

45
00:04:05,021 --> 00:04:08,696
Hey! Maybe it would be
best to rest for a moment!

46
00:04:11,741 --> 00:04:15,893
Rest, you said?
Alright, I agree! Sure!

47
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,133
What is this?

48
00:04:18,181 --> 00:04:22,379
"The silver marsh sleeps quietly
under three crescent moons.

49
00:04:22,501 --> 00:04:25,652
From the ripples of water
rises a silver ship.

50
00:04:25,701 --> 00:04:28,340
...and a silver knight
cries out to the sky:

51
00:04:28,381 --> 00:04:32,613
'The moon! The moon can help me!
The moon can give me strength!'"

52
00:04:32,661 --> 00:04:34,652
This must be the key...

53
00:04:34,701 --> 00:04:36,896
...to find
that legendary silver ship!

54
00:04:37,181 --> 00:04:40,093
What?! Which legendary
silver ship?

55
00:04:40,141 --> 00:04:43,258
That ship that no one yet knows
where it ended up.

56
00:04:43,581 --> 00:04:46,493
Exactly! And the words
written in this book...

57
00:04:46,541 --> 00:04:48,850
..could show us the place.

58
00:04:51,701 --> 00:04:54,420
So, did you manage
to find out where it could be?

59
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:56,133
Well...

60
00:04:57,661 --> 00:05:00,016
No, not exactly

61
00:05:01,181 --> 00:05:04,059
With the words from that book
it shouldn't be difficult...

62
00:05:04,101 --> 00:05:06,251
to find the silver ship.

63
00:05:10,261 --> 00:05:12,092
That's all.

64
00:05:12,541 --> 00:05:15,578
Is that silver ship
really so precious then?

65
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:20,457
Yes! And we must prevent any
evil person from taking it.

66
00:05:20,501 --> 00:05:24,016
And it worries me that
Geralamon is also aware of it.

67
00:05:27,741 --> 00:05:31,336
- I've had an idea!
- Let's hope it's a good idea

68
00:05:31,661 --> 00:05:35,336
Yes, it's a great idea! The two of us
will set out in search of the ship.

69
00:05:35,381 --> 00:05:37,576
If we find it again,
we’ll divide the treasure...

70
00:05:37,621 --> 00:05:39,816
...among all the inhabitants
of the town! Isn't it great?

71
00:05:39,861 --> 00:05:42,898
Wonderful! If we divide
the treasure among all the people,

72
00:05:42,941 --> 00:05:46,013
everyone will be rich
and Geralamon won't be able to use it

73
00:05:46,061 --> 00:05:49,815
...to perform evil deeds!
It's truly an excellent idea!

74
00:05:51,101 --> 00:05:53,092
- Well done!
- Let's look for the ship!

75
00:05:57,221 --> 00:05:59,416
Three half-moons, three half-moons...

76
00:05:59,461 --> 00:06:01,929
- The silver ship...
- Three half-moons...

77
00:06:03,061 --> 00:06:05,211
Have you perhaps found something?

78
00:06:05,261 --> 00:06:08,537
Not yet, but I must have it
at any cost.

79
00:06:09,381 --> 00:06:11,736
It's a great treasure, you know, Neelon?

80
00:06:12,021 --> 00:06:14,899
Of course I know!
And I'd want it all for myself.

81
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,413
You will find the treasure and sell it
to some other country.

82
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:21,498
With the proceeds, you'll be able to
hire a great army.

83
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:24,210
Ah, yes, if we find it.

84
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:34,015
I've got him! I've got him on the hook!

85
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:37,818
Fish, have you ever seen a
silver ship in this pond?

86
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:41,410
Yes, a big ship, all made
of silver! Tell me, have you ever seen it?

87
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,338
No? Thanks anyway.

88
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:45,611
Don't get caught again, okay? Bye!

89
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:49,778
It was the only fish I had caught
all day!

90
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:56,017
Water bird, is there by any chance a
silver ship at the bottom of the lake?

91
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:01,017
It’s not here! It’s not here!

92
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:06,379
Three half-moons, three half-moons..

93
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,298
Three half-moons...

94
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:14,449
A silver ship in a silver swamp:
but it’s absurd!

95
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:16,731
And besides, there is only one moon!

96
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:22,251
Have you solved the riddle?

97
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:25,816
Damn you Neelon, I asked
you if you solved the riddle!

98
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:28,813
- Answer!
- Greetings, Grand Duke Geralamon

99
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:32,012
- Hello, hello... - You were playing,
instead of obeying me!

100
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,291
But I’ll cut your nose off!

101
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:38,050
No! No! Not the nose! I swear to you,
I wasn't playing!

102
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:42,171
- Have you solved the enigma?
- Actually, not yet...

103
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:45,173
What do you mean "not yet"?!
You lazybones!

104
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:48,734
If I were to solve
the riddle of the three half-moons,

105
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:55,016
Finally I’ve got it!

106
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:59,895
"Half-moon" means an arch.
Three half-moons: three arches!

107
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:02,500
Look closely
at those three half-moons over there

108
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:07,334
They must mean arches or mountains
in the middle of the Northern woods!

109
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,855
I believe the silver ship
is right there.

110
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:22,370
The three crescents are actually
the peaks of those three mountains.

111
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:32,377
But there’s no marsh here!
Where is the silver marsh? Dammit!

112
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:47,091
Help! But it's full of water here!

113
00:08:47,621 --> 00:08:49,373
Help!

114
00:08:53,261 --> 00:08:56,333
It was just an illusion!
But maybe...

115
00:08:56,501 --> 00:08:58,856
...there was a marsh here
in the past.

116
00:09:01,021 --> 00:09:03,819
Just as I thought: once,
there was water here!

117
00:09:03,861 --> 00:09:07,331
I’d really like to know what it
was I had climbed onto before.

118
00:09:24,381 --> 00:09:26,895
Silver! It's silver!

119
00:09:27,381 --> 00:09:29,019
It's silver!

120
00:09:30,461 --> 00:09:35,330
Finally I found it! The silver ship
must be buried here!

121
00:09:37,701 --> 00:09:40,374
And this must be
a part of the ship!

122
00:09:44,101 --> 00:09:46,217
Yes, of course, it's the mast!

123
00:09:47,261 --> 00:09:50,731
Let's dig! Dig! Dig! Dig!
Come on, dig!

124
00:09:52,621 --> 00:09:54,737
We need a shovel!

125
00:09:59,221 --> 00:10:01,940
A shovel! A shovel! A shovel!

126
00:10:35,421 --> 00:10:39,209
Moon, answer me:
how long was I sleeping?

127
00:10:39,541 --> 00:10:41,497
Who woke me up?

128
00:10:41,621 --> 00:10:44,533
Tell me, moon, please!
And tell me:

129
00:10:44,581 --> 00:10:47,220
does evil still threaten the Earth?

130
00:10:47,581 --> 00:10:50,459
If so, give me strength!

131
00:11:07,901 --> 00:11:11,098
Listen, owl...
Could you tell me, please,

132
00:11:11,141 --> 00:11:13,609
...if you have ever heard of
a silver ship...

133
00:11:13,661 --> 00:11:16,334
...at the bottom of a silver swamp?
No?

134
00:11:17,421 --> 00:11:19,139
Thank you.

135
00:11:26,781 --> 00:11:29,056
Bye, Choppy. Goodnight

136
00:11:29,101 --> 00:11:32,889
Don't get discouraged, Sapphire.
We will go look for it again tomorrow

137
00:11:34,181 --> 00:11:35,899
- Bye!
- Bye!

138
00:11:44,181 --> 00:11:46,251
It's already night, I have to hurry!

139
00:11:49,541 --> 00:11:53,454
But there are three crescents over there!
Stop, Opal! Stop!

140
00:11:56,181 --> 00:12:00,459
Those are the Rainbow Mountains! I
understand! Hurry, Opal! Let's go!

141
00:12:21,701 --> 00:12:24,454
The three crescents
are the peaks of those mountains,

142
00:12:24,501 --> 00:12:27,220
but the swamp isn't here.
According to the words of that book,

143
00:12:27,261 --> 00:12:29,616
there should have been
a silver swamp here.

144
00:12:34,501 --> 00:12:37,777
Who are you? Why have you come?

145
00:12:38,901 --> 00:12:41,734
I am Sapphire,
the Prince of this Country!

146
00:12:41,781 --> 00:12:44,579
I have come to search
for the swamp of legend!

147
00:12:44,901 --> 00:12:48,576
Then you are a descendant
of that cursed, foolish King.

148
00:12:48,941 --> 00:12:50,897
Was it you who woke me up?

149
00:12:50,941 --> 00:12:54,013
So that silver swamp
was right here...

150
00:12:54,621 --> 00:12:57,010
I won't let you get close.

151
00:13:04,741 --> 00:13:06,811
What do you want to do?

152
00:13:32,901 --> 00:13:35,096
I'm finished..!

153
00:13:35,661 --> 00:13:39,449
Luna! Luna, help me, please!

154
00:13:39,861 --> 00:13:43,410
Please, give me strength!

155
00:13:44,701 --> 00:13:46,453
Now or never!

156
00:13:53,501 --> 00:13:55,537
What could have happened to him?

157
00:13:59,621 --> 00:14:01,612
He's disappeared! But where?

158
00:14:02,741 --> 00:14:05,813
Knight! Knight!

159
00:14:24,621 --> 00:14:27,010
Those are vampire bats!

160
00:14:27,541 --> 00:14:30,499
I must escape while this torch is burning!

161
00:14:41,461 --> 00:14:43,213
That's a door!

162
00:14:44,461 --> 00:14:46,099
Damn it!

163
00:14:51,301 --> 00:14:53,451
They're coming! I have to flee!

164
00:14:54,821 --> 00:14:56,812
I have to manage to open it!

165
00:15:09,661 --> 00:15:11,413
The ship...!

166
00:15:43,381 --> 00:15:45,576
Down! Hurry up!

167
00:15:45,621 --> 00:15:47,896
Hurry up or the sun will rise!

168
00:15:47,941 --> 00:15:50,853
Hurry up! Damn it, hurry up!

169
00:15:51,141 --> 00:15:54,213
Neelon, did it really weigh a hundred tons?

170
00:15:54,261 --> 00:15:56,775
Sure! Judging
by the height of the mast...!

171
00:15:56,821 --> 00:15:59,415
This winch, maybe,
won't be enough to pull it up!

172
00:15:59,461 --> 00:16:01,099
Really?!

173
00:16:02,501 --> 00:16:06,176
Damn, how big it is!
Even the oars are silver!

174
00:16:06,221 --> 00:16:09,019
I'll be able to share it
with all the people of the world!

175
00:16:09,141 --> 00:16:12,178
- Don't touch the ship!
- It's him! What do you want?

176
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:15,293
I will not hand over this ship to you, because
the blood of that foolish King...

177
00:16:15,341 --> 00:16:17,809
..flows in your veins!
- But who are you?

178
00:16:18,901 --> 00:16:21,495
I have been protecting this ship
for hundreds of years.

179
00:16:21,541 --> 00:16:23,611
I am a silver spirit.

180
00:16:24,181 --> 00:16:25,739
What?!

181
00:16:30,141 --> 00:16:32,814
Soon we will arrive
at the treasure swamp!

182
00:16:33,021 --> 00:16:36,252
Hurry up! Hurry up!

183
00:16:37,341 --> 00:16:39,252
Please, listen to me!

184
00:16:39,301 --> 00:16:42,611
I want to share this treasure
with all the people of the world!

185
00:16:42,901 --> 00:16:45,415
Your ancestor said the same thing,

186
00:16:45,461 --> 00:16:47,531
but then he kept everything for himself..

187
00:16:47,581 --> 00:16:50,379
..and because of him
many wars were fought

188
00:16:50,421 --> 00:16:52,889
...and thousands of lives
were destroyed.

189
00:16:53,101 --> 00:16:55,331
That's why I stole
the King's silver!

190
00:16:55,381 --> 00:16:58,100
Now my spirit
dwells in this armor

191
00:16:58,141 --> 00:17:00,177
..to protect this ship

192
00:17:00,221 --> 00:17:02,530
I won't be fooled
by your words!

193
00:17:02,581 --> 00:17:06,415
I don't want to deceive you! For myself
I want neither the silver, nor the jewels!

194
00:17:06,461 --> 00:17:08,577
I only want to share them with the poor

195
00:17:08,621 --> 00:17:11,738
I beg you to believe me,
I swear to you that is what I'll do!

196
00:17:12,621 --> 00:17:14,452
Shut up!

197
00:17:18,501 --> 00:17:21,140
Silver spirit,
listen to me, please!

198
00:17:21,181 --> 00:17:23,820
I don't want the gold, the silver
or the jewels!

199
00:17:23,861 --> 00:17:26,250
I only want to divide them
among the poor!

200
00:17:26,301 --> 00:17:29,020
Silver spirit,
are you listening to me?

201
00:17:29,301 --> 00:17:32,930
Silver spirit!
Silver spirit!

202
00:17:36,661 --> 00:17:38,652
Where could he have gone?

203
00:17:51,901 --> 00:17:54,210
But your body isn't...!

204
00:17:54,901 --> 00:17:57,779
Only my spirit
dwells in this armor,

205
00:17:57,821 --> 00:18:01,416
to prevent anyone from throwing
the world into chaos with this silver!

206
00:18:08,741 --> 00:18:10,572
Look out!

207
00:18:16,021 --> 00:18:18,455
You helped me.
Why?

208
00:18:51,661 --> 00:18:54,619
- Silver spirit!
- Prince...

209
00:18:54,901 --> 00:18:58,177
- You've come to your senses.
- I have to ask you a favor.

210
00:19:00,581 --> 00:19:04,369
Some foolish men have come
to take the silver ship.

211
00:19:10,621 --> 00:19:14,375
- Lower the crane!
- Lower the crane!

212
00:19:19,381 --> 00:19:22,020
I cannot move
without the moonlight.

213
00:19:22,141 --> 00:19:26,020
Wear this armor in my place
and protect the silver ship.

214
00:19:26,141 --> 00:19:29,178
This armor is lighter than a
feather and stronger than iron.

215
00:19:29,261 --> 00:19:31,934
- It will protect you.
- Yes, I know.

216
00:19:36,301 --> 00:19:38,861
It seems we have hooked
the ship, Neelon?

217
00:19:38,901 --> 00:19:41,461
Yes, of course! Hoist the crane!

218
00:19:41,541 --> 00:19:44,738
- Hoist the crane!
- Come on!

219
00:19:51,701 --> 00:19:53,498
Hurry up!

220
00:20:01,701 --> 00:20:03,896
There it is, it's coming up!

221
00:20:14,541 --> 00:20:16,691
That's the silver ship!

222
00:20:16,741 --> 00:20:19,414
Don't waste time!
Hurry up and pull it up!

223
00:20:24,901 --> 00:20:26,857
What is it?

224
00:20:27,221 --> 00:20:30,418
Just as I thought! You're
quite a bunch of thugs, you lot!

225
00:20:31,581 --> 00:20:33,697
And who are you?

226
00:20:34,581 --> 00:20:37,812
I am the silver knight,
the guardian of this ship,

227
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:39,738
and I will not surrender it to you!

228
00:20:39,781 --> 00:20:42,136
Kill that monster immediately
with arrows!

229
00:20:45,141 --> 00:20:47,291
Now I’m coming!

230
00:20:47,821 --> 00:20:49,812
Here I am!

231
00:20:58,821 --> 00:21:02,177
It’s useless! You cannot penetrate
my armor with bows or arrows!

232
00:21:02,541 --> 00:21:05,135
- He’s a monster! Let’s flee!
- Wait for me!

233
00:21:13,701 --> 00:21:15,657
Let’s run away! He’s coming!

234
00:21:15,701 --> 00:21:17,896
Quick, behind here!
Don’t let yourself be seen!

235
00:21:18,901 --> 00:21:20,653
Neelon!

236
00:21:21,541 --> 00:21:24,453
- What is he doing?
- He’s fighting with the soldiers, down there

237
00:21:24,501 --> 00:21:27,174
I’ve got it!
Let’s release the brakes on this winch.

238
00:21:27,221 --> 00:21:29,735
...and we’ll crush him under it!
- Yes!

239
00:21:44,621 --> 00:21:46,612
- Hurray!
- We did it!

240
00:22:05,101 --> 00:22:07,217
The water is coming out!

241
00:22:15,021 --> 00:22:18,696
Let’s run! Let’s run!
Otherwise we’ll drown!

242
00:22:32,341 --> 00:22:34,218
Finally on dry land!

243
00:22:36,541 --> 00:22:40,011
How could you dare
return up before me?!

244
00:22:43,781 --> 00:22:47,330
It’s your fault that we didn’t manage
to take the silver, damn it!

245
00:22:48,421 --> 00:22:50,571
Shut up and let me up!

246
00:22:50,901 --> 00:22:53,051
- No, you won’t go up first!
- Yes, I will!

247
00:22:53,101 --> 00:22:54,819
No, you ugly...

248
00:23:04,061 --> 00:23:06,450
Prince, thanks to you
I was able to protect...

249
00:23:06,501 --> 00:23:08,492
...the silver ship
from those thugs.

250
00:23:08,541 --> 00:23:10,418
- I will give it to you.
- What?!

251
00:23:11,461 --> 00:23:14,214
The silver ship
is your treasure, now.

252
00:23:14,381 --> 00:23:17,930
But until you are King and have
brought peace to your country,

253
00:23:17,981 --> 00:23:20,017
I will keep it at the bottom of the lake

254
00:23:20,301 --> 00:23:24,010
I will watch you from this silver
swamp... until then.

255
00:23:26,421 --> 00:23:30,653
Wait for me, please! I will not fail
to bring peace to my country.

256
00:23:35,021 --> 00:23:39,651
Remember: until then,
I will watch you from this swamp!

257
00:24:14,061 --> 00:24:17,681
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

258
